# AI-103 Lesson 14 -- copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# THREE hostnames, ONE Azure account. This is the single most common way to
# lose twenty minutes in this lesson, so read the list before you edit anything.
#
#   *.openai.azure.com            chat and vision      (scripts append /openai/v1)
#   *.cognitiveservices.azure.com Content Safety       <- Beat 1 and Beat 2 live here
#   *.services.ai.azure.com       Content Understanding (Lesson 13's host)
#
# Send an image:analyze payload to the openai.azure.com host and you get a 404
# with no explanation. Confirm what your account publishes with:
#
#   az cognitiveservices account show -n <account> -g <rg> --query properties.endpoints
#
# Verified live against this account 2026-08-12.

# --- Foundry chat / vision (Beat 2 OCR, Beat 3 structured findings) -----------
FOUNDRY_ACCOUNT_ENDPOINT=https://<your-account>.openai.azure.com
CHAT_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# --- Content Safety (Beat 1 image filter, Beat 2 Prompt Shields) -------------
# Note the host. It is NOT the same as the line above.
CONTENT_SAFETY_ENDPOINT=https://<your-account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com

# RBAC: your signed-in identity needs Cognitive Services User on the account.
# Owner is NOT enough -- Owner is a control-plane role and these are data-plane
# calls. A 403 here means the role, not the endpoint.
#
#   az role assignment create --assignee <you@domain> \
#     --role "Cognitive Services User" --scope <account resource id>
